<statement>
<p>It is estimated that 59.9<percent/> of Kickstarter projects are successfully funded. Assume each Kickstarter project is independent. A random sample of 16 Kickstarter projects are followed. Let <m>\displaystyle{X}</m> be the number Kickstarter projects that are successfully funded. Calculate the following:</p>
<p>a. <m>\displaystyle\mu_{{X}}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>b. <m>\displaystyle\sigma_{{X}}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>c. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}={10}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>d. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}{<}{11}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>e. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}{>}{8}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>f.  <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}\geq{8}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>g. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({8}\leq{X}\leq{11}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="20" /></p>

</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>9.584</li><li>1.9604040399877</li><li>0.19799696083466</li><li>0.67412837450809</li><li>0.71322413645234</li><li>0.85583351942168</li><li>0.6912861009676</li></ul></p>
</answer>

